# PR Conduct

PR descriptions must be direct, concise, and linked to the plan.

- No apologetic prose, padding, or "quick aside" language.
- Always link to the relevant plan section or phase.
- State exactly what changed, why it was required, and how it was verified (tests, manual run, CI).
- Never bury unfinished work behind "for now", "out of scope", "follow-up PR", or placeholder comments.
- If the PR deviates from the plan, call out the deviation and obtain explicit approval via plan update first.